'''''Geranium pyrenaicum''''', otherwise known as '''hedgerow cranesbill''' or '''mountain cranesbill'''<ref>{{cite web |title=Geranium pyrenaicum |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/23113/Geranium-pyrenaicum/Details |website=RHS |accessdate=14 June 2020}}</ref> is a perennial species of plant in the family [[Geraniaceae]]. 
It can be found on roadside verges and along hedgerows.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Sterry |first1=Paul |title=Complete Guide to British Wild Flowers |date=2006 |publisher=Collins |isbn=9780007814848 |page=98-99}}</ref>

==Distribution==
It is probably introduced in England and Wales, where it is fairly common.<ref>{{cite web |title=Geranium pyrenaicum |url=https://www.ukwildflowers.com/Web_pages/geranium_pyrenaicum_hedgerow_cranesbill.htm |website=UK Wild Flowers |accessdate=14 June 2020}}</ref> Elsewhere, it can be found in the southern Alps, the Pyrenees and the Caucasus.

